      "value": "In case of, from theghost87 on Discord : \"Okay, I just went to read it. So, to give you more information about this bug : what's happening is with Udon's \"respawn\" function. Normally, before the update that broke everything, objects would be returned to their original location once the respawn function was triggered. Now, this is no longer the case. With this update, objects will respawn where the player loaded them. So, if someone picks up a pen and hides it before entering the map, its respawn location will be where it was hidden.\"",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
